/Title (The chain remembers across sessions. Your transition probabilities from last week are in there, weighted less than today's but still present. If you spent a month playing aggressively and just came back after a break, the chain has both versions of you- the aggressive one and whatever you are now; the weights are decided between them by recency. The first 10 minutes of a returning session are the most dangerous. The chain is running on old you while you're still figuring out what you currently are.)
